cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >
  If you use Resonance in your research or build on its protocol specification,
  please cite it using the metadata below.

title: "Resonance: A Privacy-First Acoustic Incident Detection Platform"
type: software

version: "4.0.0"
date-released: "2025-08-25"

abstract: >
  Resonance is an open-source distributed acoustic incident detection platform
  designed for privacy-preserving deployment in public spaces. It detects
  impulsive acoustic events (gunshots, vehicle impacts, glass breaking,
  explosions) using networked edge nodes with directional microphone arrays.
  The system produces Acoustic Probability Surfaces for localization, supports
  deterministic replay for auditability, and enforces privacy constraints at
  the type-system and protocol level. No speech recognition, speaker
  identification, or continuous audio recording is possible by design.

authors:
  - name: "Resonance Contributors"
    website: "https://github.com/resonance-project/resonance"

repository-code: "https://github.com/resonance-project/resonance"
url: "https://resonance-project.example"
license: Apache-2.0

keywords:
  - acoustic-sensing
  - gunshot-detection
  - edge-computing
  - privacy-by-design
  - distributed-systems
  - signal-processing
  - MFCC
  - direction-of-arrival
  - Ed25519
  - microphone-array
  - spatial-intelligence
  - IoT

